The inverse FFT can be computed efficiently using the conjugate method:
1. **Conjugate the input**: $\text{conj}(x[n])$
2. **Apply forward FFT**: $X[k] = \text{FFT}(x[n])$
3. **Conjugate output and normalize**: $x_{\text{ifft}}[n] = \frac{1}{N} \text{conj}(X[k])$

